<!--Post: 1809--><!--Time: 1102901518-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1809"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Moondog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Moondog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 5:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Listed below is a link with some fuzzy images of the purported puzzles mailed by BTK to KAKE TV.  Has anyone been able to recontruct these or possess cleaner copies than those listed at the bottom of the page? <BR>  Also, what are the details surrounding the puzzle displayed between the photos of Charlie Otero &amp; Nancy Fox on this website&#39;s &#39;news&#39; section?  Did BTK mail this to the media, and if so, when?  The clues are very apparent: bkt = btk, clu = clue, dmv = department of motor vehicles, fox = Nancy Fox.   <BR>Any information would be greatly appreciated. <BR> <BR><a href="http://p216.ezboard.com/fcrimeandjustice13552frm100.showMessage?topicID=559.topic" target=_top>http://p216.ezboard.com/fcrimeandjustice13552frm10 0.showMessage?topicID=559.topic</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1809-->
<!--Post: 1831--><!--Time: 1102967272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1831"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 11:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t have a real clear picture of it yet but some observations. <BR>1. It&#39;s titled &#34;Chapter 8&#34;. I wonder if this feeds back to an earlier link by BTK, in which he appeared to align a set of chapter titles to the story of the case at the crime library. <BR>Crimelibrary..8. Cold case Squad. BTK.. 8. Mo-ID Ruse. <BR> <BR>2. It appears to be something like the first Zodiac cipher in construction, in as much as it appear to have 3 sections &#40;all on the one page&#41; <BR>Here we have blocks of 13X9 in the first two section and maybe 13X 11 in the final third &#40;don&#39;t have a full picture&#41;Some spaces are also blank though. <BR> <BR>3.At first glance we have various words spelled vertically,horizontally and perhaps some anagrams. <BR>Most appear to tie back to earlier information provided by BTK. <BR> <BR>Cruise/I follow &#40;Mr NL ?&#41;/ spot victims/ details/ telephone/ realtor/ helm ...are a few of the most obvious thus far.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1831-->
<!--Post: 1832--><!--Time: 1102968950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1832"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 12:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually, now that I look a little closer, in the top left hand corner of section 1, we have the first two letter MO linked underneath with the words &#34;Cruise&#34; and &#34;Prowl&#34;. <BR>Don&#39;t have the middle section but at the top left hand corner of section three we have &#34;Ruse&#34; linked with &#34;Realtor&#34;.  <BR>Maybe it does tie back to the MO-ID RUSE. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1832-->
<!--Post: 1840--><!--Time: 1102998385-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Moondog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Moondog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 8:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good eye Sean.  To the right of the word &#34;realtor&#34; appear to be the words &#34;insurer&#34; and &#34;service&#34;.  Also, I believe the word &#34;fantasies&#34; appears in the third column beginning with the fifth letter from the top, and the word &#34;follow&#34; appears upside down near the top of the page in the fourth column from the left.  Many of the letters in the middle of the page are subscripted or superscripted with numbers.  Does anyone have more information &#40;i.e. were there multiple pages and when this/these were received&#41; or a clean&#40;er&#41; copy of this puzzle?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
