<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1845"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:btk@mikecole.org" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_cole<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_cole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 10:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe &#34;telephone&#34; is actually part of the phrase &#34;telephone co&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1845-->
<!--Post: 1851--><!--Time: 1103024896-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1851"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flaco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flaco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 3:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Help!  It may be my tired eyes but I&#39;ve searched this site for the letter containing the &#34;dudes&#34; reference from the killer.  Is it on here and I missed it? Or is it public knowledge and I&#39;m too tired at 4:45 am to find it?  Thanks1!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1851-->
<!--Post: 1860--><!--Time: 1103050178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1860"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 10:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi All. <BR> <BR>Here are the puzzles.  BTK sent KAKETV this puzzle around May 5th.  KAKETV showed some of the puzzle as background for their story on BTK&#39;s latest communication.  There were several people that recorded the newscast and made copies of the pictures of the puzzle to enhance.  All the letters are not known because of the Channel 10 logo on the TV.  Lighting and angles ended up blocking some of the letters, etc. WPD has never verified that what KAKE showed on TV was an actual copy of the puzzle or a prop.  I talked to one of the officers on the tip line who could not verify, but he did say that he didn&#39;t think that KAKE would have time to make up a prop puzzle for the newscast.  Some of the letters have been best guess but they were arrived at by several people independently. If a letter is in red, that is a pretty good bet. If a letter is in blue, it is probable.  If a letter is in black, that is a blue letter I have made black to fit my theory.  A question mark means there is no consensus on the letter.  A number sign means a number with no consensus.  Any way, here is a post I wrote concerning the puzzle and my theory.  The puzzle grids are in reverse order.  I chose to talk about the third grid first, etc. because it was easier to illustrate the theory.  That makes sense in itself because it might mean that BTK got lazier when it came time to make the third puzzle.  Thanks. <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- --------------------------------  <BR> <BR> <BR>I have been playing around with the puzzle and reviewing old posts. I believe Rsquared suggested that the puzzle might have been laid out in excel because the numbers in the puzzle were off center. BTK is about 50-60. Because of his age and background, he probably just has a rudimentary knowledge of excel or he would have known how to center the numbers. So, I think that Rsquared was probably correct. This puzzle was written in excel on a computer keyboard.  <BR> <BR>Since BTK has just a rudimentary knowledge of excel, I am making a supposition that all words to be found in the puzzle are either horizontal or vertical. There are no diagonal words. There are no scrambled words. There are no words to be made by changing directions. Everything is straightforward, either horizontal or vertical.  <BR> <BR>So, BTK sat down with his computer. He opened up excel. He made a blank grid and started writing. He placed the words and phrases he wanted you to find in the grid. If it were a layered puzzle, he would add his message at this time. Then he would fill in all the other blanks with random filler letters.  <BR> <BR>Normally you would use filler letters to lead people astray. For example you would put in other words that were not part of the puzzle or you could make a long word, but have the last letter wrong, etc. Mr. A made the observation that some of the filler letters were obviously from rows on the keyboard. BTK probably just filled letters according to the keyboard. This makes sense when you see the emerging pattern many times in the puzzle.  <BR> <BR>Let’s take a look at the RUSE grid &#40;number 3&#41;. <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915rusea.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915rusea.JPG</a> <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR>The words we have are RUSE, REALTOR, INSURANCE, SERVICEMAN, HANDYMAN, WRONG ADDRESS, LOST DOG, REMODEL, HELP, FAKE ID, FOR SALE, TAG. All these words are highlighted in yellow. Once you have these words highlighted, lets turn to the fillers. I have these highlighted in light green. You start at the top and go horizontally in order of the keyboard.  <BR> <BR>Line 1&#41; T Y U I continue Line 2&#41; with O P. The next line on the keyboard would be A S D. Drop down to  <BR>Line 4&#41; then continue across the keyboard F G H J. Drop down to Line 5&#41; continue across the keyboard with K and L. <BR> <BR>All of the filler letters are dead. They cannot be used with other letters to form words. Any words you get from filler letters are coincidence. They are not BTK’s words. <BR> <BR>I used purpleghostie’s suggested letters to make TAG and FORSALE which I included. BTK could have used a lost TAG ruse to stop someone in an automobile. &#40;He was probably the one that removed it.&#41; He might have answered a FORSALE ad in the Eagle and showed up at someone&#39;s door.  <BR> <BR>Let’s take a look at the ID grid &#40;number 2&#41;. <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915ida.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915ida.JPG</a> <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR>I have highlighted the following words in yellow. We have ID, TELEPHONE CO, ANDERSON, LARRY, SCHOOL, OFFICER, WICHITA, and STRONG.  <BR> <BR>The filler letters are once again filled with a green background. In column 2 we have a familiar combination. It is the top of the keyboard. Q W E R T Y U I. This eliminates WPD and POET from the puzzle. I believe they are now a coincidence. Column 9 going down reads F G H J K L, which is still more filler. In Row 5 you can see S D F. In Row 6 you can see Z X C, then down to B. Go down 2 rows and you have D F G H J K. Go up one square for the L. The bottom line is M N B V. I believe that all of this is filler. In column one we have F H L K. I am assuming this is filler because of the close proximity of keyboard letters.  <BR> <BR>On this grid I have substituted number signs for the question marks where I believe there should be numbers. This goes back to the original theory of why the numbers are off center. I do not think they are fillers because they are non-sequential on the keyboard or calculator. I believe that the numbers represent something. 316 is probably a reference to the area code. If the top set of numbers turn out to be 293 then you could possibly have the phone number 316-293-2643. This is the telephone number for <BR> <BR>University of Kansas School of Medicine-Wichita <BR>1010 N. Kansas <BR>Wichita, Kansas 67214 <BR>316-293-2643 <BR> <BR>About the time that BTK surfaced this year the University of Kansas School of Medicine-Wichita was hosting a Live &amp; Learn lecture series entitled &#34;Chronic Illness, Acute Answers&#34; &#34;Different Strokes: A Look at Cerebrovascular Disease&#34;.  There is also a Larry Anderson affiliated with the University which is contained in the puzzle. <BR> <BR>&#40;I kind of got off on a tangent here. That is the danger of trying to read too much into these things.&#41; <BR> <BR>The numbers could also be an ID number of someone, or a social security number, or an address. The list goes on and on.  <BR> <BR>Let’s take a look at the MO grid &#40;number 1&#41;. <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR><a href="http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915moa.JPG" target=_top>http://pages.prodigy.net/cross/puz915moa.JPG</a> <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR>Once again I have highlighted the words in yellow. You will find MO, CRUISE, SEX, PROWL, FANTASIES, FOLLOW, SPOT, VICTIM, DETAILS, PLAN, STEAM BUILDS, and I GO FOR IT.  <BR> <BR>I have highlighted all the filler in light green.  <BR> <BR>I have been wondering about Row 10. Starting with Column 8 and going backwards the letters read L B T T R S. I am wondering if the B could be and E and BTK misspelled LETTERS as LETTRS. <BR> <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR> <BR>Once you have the words and filler highlighted, what do you do with the rest of the puzzle? If the puzzle is layered and if the puzzle contains a message, then anything that is not yellow and green should make up the message. But we have 2 problems. We do not have all of the letters or numbers to determine if there are additional words, phrases, or filler. The second problem is that BTK could have used random filler to finish.  <BR> <BR>If there is a hidden message in this puzzle, I believe there are a couple of possibilities.  <BR> <BR> <BR>1&#41;. Letters that do not constitute words or filler make up the message. <BR> <BR>2&#41;. The numbers in the ID grid refers you to the letters of the message. <BR> <BR>3&#41;. When BTK set this up in excel, maybe the RUSE grid actually had 13 rows, just like the other two puzzles. But in this grid, Row 13 contains 9 blanks for the 9 letters that make up a message. It could be as simple as one letter per column.  <BR> <BR>I left the corner Xs alone. I think there is some significance to the Xs, but I do not think that the Xs denotes the victims because some of the letters that you have to use are either words or filler. I think this is just a coincidence.  <BR> <BR>Anyway, sorry for the long post. I hope it is interesting. I would appreciate any help, comments, and/or suggestions or ideas based upon my suppositions. You can probably see things that I can’t. <BR> <BR>Mark<!--/Text--></td></tr>
